493:
When appointed, the director of emergency management is charged:
(1) To represent the governing officials of the city and the county on matters pertaining to emergency management;
(2) With assisting county and city officials in organizing county and city resources for emergency operations;
(3) With developing in conjunction with the city and county departments, the Waycross-Ware County basic plan for emergency functions set forth in section 14-19. Such plan will be consonant with the state emergency plan and shall be submitted to the county commission and/or city commission for approval and thence to the state director for approval;
(4) With maintaining the emergency management agency in carrying out the day-to-day administration of the county emergency management and disaster program including the rendering of required reports to the state emergency management office;
(5) Rendering reports such as financial, daily activity, etc., as required by governing officials in keeping with good business practices;
(6) Procuring, with the consent of governing officials, a facility to be used as the city-county emergency operating center; and
(7) During periods of a declared emergency, and under the supervision of city and county governing officials, coordinate the activities of the city-county emergency operating center staff.
(Code 1977, § 9-20; Ord. of 6-20-1972, § II; Ord. No. 78-22, § II, 9-19-1978; Ord. No. 80-6, § II, 2-19-1980; Ord. No. 93-29, § 1D, 12-6-1993)

505:
